1
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:14,310
Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:20,230
Welcome back to Business English Podcast. Hello, everyone, and thanks for joining us today.

3
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:21,230
I'm Daniel.

4
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:26,630
And I'm Sophia. We're here to help you learn natural, practical English that you can use

5
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:28,350
every day at work.

6
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:33,590
Our goal is to make English learning simple, useful, and realistic.

7
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:36,130
This topic is extremely important.

8
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:38,930
How to talk about job tasks in English.

9
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:43,330
Yes, this is something you do every single day at work.

10
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:47,850
You talk about what you're doing, what you finished, what you still need to do, and

11
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:49,530
what problems you have.

12
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:50,530
Exactly.

13
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:55,190
Whether you're talking to your boss, your coworkers, or even clients, you need the

14
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:58,730
right phrases to describe your tasks clearly.

15
00:00:58,730 --> 00:01:03,810
And today, we're going to show you all of this through natural conversation, just like

16
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:04,810
real life.

17
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:09,330
So, if you find this helpful, don't forget to practice along with us.

18
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:11,210
Alright, are you ready?

19
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:12,210
Let's get started.

20
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:14,650
Hey, Daniel, how are you today?

21
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,530
I'm doing well, thanks.

22
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:20,370
But honestly, I have a lot of tasks to finish today.

23
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:22,530
It's going to be a busy day.

24
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:23,530
Same here.

25
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:25,930
I made a long to-do list this morning.

26
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:27,770
Oh, I do that too.

27
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:32,730
helps me stay organized. Exactly. So what's on your list today?

28
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:39,490
Well, first I need to reply to emails, then I have to prepare a report, and later I have

29
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:44,450
a meeting with the team. That sounds like a full schedule. What about you? What are

30
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:49,890
you working on today? I'm currently working on a presentation for a client. I also need

31
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:56,130
to update a spreadsheet and finish a document before the deadline. Wow, that's a lot.

32
00:01:56,130 --> 00:01:59,410
Let's imagine we're in the office starting our day.

33
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,810
Good morning, Sophia.

34
00:02:00,810 --> 00:02:02,150
Good morning, Daniel.

35
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:03,570
What are you working on today?

36
00:02:03,570 --> 00:02:06,170
I'm focusing on the sales report this morning.

37
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:10,210
I need to analyze the data and summarize the results.

38
00:02:10,210 --> 00:02:11,570
That sounds important.

39
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:12,650
When does it do?

40
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:16,450
The deadline is tomorrow, so I need to finish it today.

41
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:17,450
Good luck.

42
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:18,930
Let me know if you need any help.

43
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:19,930
Thanks.

44
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:20,930
I appreciate it.

45
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:21,930
Hey, Daniel.

46
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:22,930
Do you have a minute?

47
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:23,930
Sure.

48
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:24,930
What's up?

49
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:29,930
complete this task, but I'm not sure what to do next. Could you take a look?

50
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:31,810
Of course. Let me see.

51
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:36,690
I've already finished the first part, but I'm confused about the second part.

52
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:41,730
I see. You just need to follow the same structure as the first section.

53
00:02:41,730 --> 00:02:43,610
Oh, that makes sense now.

54
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:48,810
Sometimes tasks seem complicated, but they're actually simple once you understand them.

55
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:51,010
That's true. Thanks for your help.

56
00:02:51,010 --> 00:02:53,850
Hey, Sophia, can I give you a quick update?

57
00:02:53,850 --> 00:02:54,610
Sure.

58
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:57,050
I've completed the first part of the project,

59
00:02:57,050 --> 00:02:59,690
and now I'm working on the second phase.

60
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:01,210
That's great progress.

61
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:03,050
I think I'll be able to finish everything

62
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:04,410
by the end of the day.

63
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:05,210
Perfect.

64
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:06,450
Keep me posted.

65
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:09,170
Hey, Daniel, how's your presentation going?

66
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:10,250
It's going well.

67
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,290
I finished most of the slides,

68
00:03:12,290 --> 00:03:15,450
but I still need to add some data and visuals.

69
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:16,490
That's important.

70
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:19,250
Visuals make presentations clearer.

71
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:20,210
Exactly.

72
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:22,610
I'm planning to finish it this afternoon.

73
00:03:22,610 --> 00:03:23,610
Sounds good.

74
00:03:23,610 --> 00:03:26,150
Let's talk about multitasking.

75
00:03:26,150 --> 00:03:28,850
Oh yes, that happens a lot at work.

76
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:31,310
Hey Daniel, what are you doing right now?

77
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:34,730
I'm answering emails while reviewing a document.

78
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:36,730
Wow, you're multitasking.

79
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:39,490
I have to, there's too much work today.

80
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:43,290
Same here, I'm handling two tasks at the same time.

81
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:46,050
Hey Sophia, I think I made a mistake.

82
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:47,130
What happened?

83
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:49,010
I was working on the spreadsheet

84
00:03:49,010 --> 00:03:51,010
and I entered the wrong data.

85
00:03:51,010 --> 00:03:53,330
Don't worry, these things happen.

86
00:03:53,330 --> 00:03:54,330
Can you fix it?

87
00:03:54,330 --> 00:03:56,330
Yes, I'm correcting it now.

88
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:59,330
Good. It's important to fix mistakes quickly.

89
00:03:59,330 --> 00:04:02,830
Hey Daniel, can you help me prioritize my tasks?

90
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:04,830
Sure. What do you have to do?

91
00:04:04,830 --> 00:04:09,830
I need to finish a report, reply to emails, and prepare for a meeting.

92
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:17,830
I'd say start with the report since it has a deadline, then reply to emails and prepare for the meeting last.

93
00:04:17,830 --> 00:04:18,830
That makes sense.

94
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:21,830
Prioritizing tasks is very important.

95
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:24,230
Yes, it helps reduce stress.

96
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:27,030
Hey Sophia, are you done with your report?

97
00:04:27,030 --> 00:04:30,130
Not yet. I'm still working on the final section.

98
00:04:30,130 --> 00:04:32,030
Do you think you'll finish it today?

99
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:33,830
Yes, I'm almost done.

100
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:34,630
Great!

101
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:37,030
Hey Daniel, can you review my work?

102
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:38,630
Sure, send it to me.

103
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:42,530
I just want to make sure everything is correct before I submit it.

104
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:45,030
That's a good idea. I'll check it now.

105
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:45,830
Thanks.

106
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:49,930
Hey Sophia, I've reviewed your report. It looks really good.

107
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:52,330
Thank you. Did you find any mistakes?

108
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:55,930
Just a few small ones, but overall it's excellent.

109
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:59,770
I appreciate your feedback. Let's talk about deadlines again.

110
00:04:59,770 --> 00:05:02,810
Yes, deadlines are very important.

111
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:05,690
Hey Daniel, are you on track with your tasks?

112
00:05:05,690 --> 00:05:09,450
Yes, I'm making good progress. I should meet the deadline.

113
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:11,530
That's great. What about you?

114
00:05:11,530 --> 00:05:14,890
I'm a bit behind schedule, but I'm catching up.

115
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:16,330
Do you need any help?

116
00:05:16,330 --> 00:05:17,850
Maybe later. Thanks.

117
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:21,450
Hey Sophia, I'm having some difficulty with this task.

118
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:22,650
What's the problem?

119
00:05:22,650 --> 00:05:25,550
I don't fully understand the instructions.

120
00:05:25,550 --> 00:05:27,550
You should ask for clarification.

121
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:29,650
Yes, I'll talk to the manager.

122
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:31,750
Hey Daniel, how did it go?

123
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:37,050
Much better. I asked for clarification and now I understand what to do.

124
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:40,950
Good. Asking questions is always better than guessing.

125
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:44,550
Hey Sophia, I've just finished my tasks for the day.

126
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:47,750
That's great. I still have a few things to complete.

127
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:48,950
Do you want help?

128
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,950
Yes, that would be amazing.

129
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:52,950
Alright, what can I do?

130
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:54,950
Can you help me organize this data?

131
00:05:54,950 --> 00:05:55,950
Sure.

132
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:59,550
Thanks for helping me. Now I can finish everything on time.

133
00:05:59,550 --> 00:06:03,050
No problem. Teamwork makes everything easier.

134
00:06:03,050 --> 00:06:04,250
Absolutely.

135
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:07,950
Hey Sophia, let's quickly go over tomorrow's tasks.

136
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,050
Good idea.

137
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:13,350
I need to start a new project and attend two meetings.

138
00:06:13,350 --> 00:06:17,150
I have to finalize a document and follow up with the client.

139
00:06:17,150 --> 00:06:19,650
Sounds like another busy day.

140
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:20,950
Definitely.

141
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:25,750
Hey, Daniel. Before we finish, can we summarize what we've learned today?

142
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:29,650
Sure. We talked about how to describe tasks like,

143
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:33,850
I'm working on a report or I need to finish this today.

144
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:36,450
We also talked about giving updates like,

145
00:06:36,450 --> 00:06:39,350
I've completed this or I'm still working on it.

146
00:06:39,350 --> 00:06:42,950
And asking for help like, could you help me with this?

147
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:45,250
Plus handling problems like,

148
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,330
I made a mistake or I need clarification.

149
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:53,450
Exactly. These are all real phrases you'll use every day at work.

150
00:06:53,450 --> 00:06:57,930
And remember, the key is to be clear, polite, and confident.

151
00:06:57,930 --> 00:07:02,230
Don't worry about perfect grammar. Focus on communication.

152
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:05,530
Practice these conversations and you'll improve quickly.

153
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:08,090
Alright everyone, that's all for today.

154
00:07:08,090 --> 00:07:09,730
Thank you so much for listening.

155
00:07:09,730 --> 00:07:12,890
Keep practicing and keep improving your English.

156
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,330
Have a great day at work.

157
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:15,330
Good-bye.

158
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:16,330
Bye.

159
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:18,530
Welcome back to Business English Podcast.

160
00:07:18,530 --> 00:07:20,690
Hello, and thanks for listening today.

161
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,850
I'm Leo.

162
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:22,850
And I'm Tina.

163
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:28,090
We're here to help you learn natural conversational English and feel confident using it in real

164
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:29,090
life.

165
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:34,410
Our goal is to make English learning simple, practical, and useful for your daily work

166
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:35,410
life.

167
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:39,050
Today we have a very important and practical topic.

168
00:07:39,050 --> 00:07:41,570
How to talk about job tasks in English.

169
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:42,570
Yes.

170
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:45,330
something you need every single day at work.

171
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:48,290
You always need to explain what you are doing,

172
00:07:48,290 --> 00:07:51,090
what you finished, what you will do next,

173
00:07:51,090 --> 00:07:53,530
and sometimes what problems you have.

174
00:07:53,530 --> 00:07:54,530
Exactly.

175
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:56,330
Whether you are talking to your boss,

176
00:07:56,330 --> 00:07:59,030
your coworkers, or even clients,

177
00:07:59,030 --> 00:08:01,450
you need to clearly describe your tasks.

178
00:08:01,450 --> 00:08:04,650
And today we are going to show you a long, natural,

179
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:07,970
and detailed conversation full of real examples.

180
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:11,210
No subtopics, just continuous conversation,

181
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:12,450
just like real life.

182
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:17,950
So, listen carefully, repeat the phrases, and imagine yourself using them at work.

183
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:19,790
All right, let's get started.

184
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,630
Hey Tina, how are you today?

185
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:24,590
Hi Leo, I'm doing well, thanks. How about you?

186
00:08:24,590 --> 00:08:27,910
I'm good, but I have a lot of tasks to handle today.

187
00:08:27,910 --> 00:08:30,690
Same here, it's one of those busy days.

188
00:08:30,690 --> 00:08:34,310
Yeah, I just sat down and started reviewing my task list.

189
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:37,750
That's a good habit. I always make it to-do list in the morning.

190
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:40,870
Me too, it helps me stay organized and focused.

191
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:42,870
So, what are you working on today?

192
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:46,990
Well, first I need to finish updating the weekly report.

193
00:08:46,990 --> 00:08:49,550
Oh right, the report you were working on yesterday.

194
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:50,670
Yes, exactly.

195
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:52,110
I completed most of it,

196
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:54,430
but I still need to add the latest data.

197
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:55,590
That makes sense.

198
00:08:55,590 --> 00:08:57,110
After that, what's next?

199
00:08:57,110 --> 00:09:00,110
After that, I need to reply to some client emails

200
00:09:00,110 --> 00:09:02,390
and then prepare for the afternoon meeting.

201
00:09:02,390 --> 00:09:04,310
That sounds like a full schedule.

202
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,270
It is.

203
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:06,150
What about you?

204
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:08,230
What tasks are you handling today?

205
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:13,230
I'm currently working on organizing project files and updating our shared documents.

206
00:09:13,230 --> 00:09:17,230
That sounds important. Keeping everything organized saves time later.

207
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:21,230
Exactly. I'm also responsible for scheduling meetings this week.

208
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:24,230
Oh, that can be tricky sometimes.

209
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:27,230
Yes, especially when everyone has different availability.

210
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:33,230
Hey Tina, quick question. How do you usually explain your tasks to your manager?

211
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:35,230
I try to be clear and structured.

212
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:40,070
I usually say what I'm working on, what I've completed, and what I'll do next.

213
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:41,070
That's a good approach.

214
00:09:41,070 --> 00:09:45,810
For example, I might say, I've completed the first part of the project and now I'm working

215
00:09:45,810 --> 00:09:47,470
on the final section.

216
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:49,630
That sounds very clear and professional.

217
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:53,070
Yes, and if there's a problem, I also mention it.

218
00:09:53,070 --> 00:09:55,870
Right, it's important to communicate challenges.

219
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:56,870
Exactly.

220
00:09:56,870 --> 00:10:01,350
For example, I might say, I'm having some difficulty with the data analysis,

221
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,390
so I may need more time.

222
00:10:03,390 --> 00:10:04,750
That's honest and helpful.

223
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:06,990
Tina, can I run something by you?

224
00:10:06,990 --> 00:10:08,150
Sure, go ahead.

225
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:11,270
I'm trying to explain my tasks better during meetings,

226
00:10:11,270 --> 00:10:13,590
but sometimes I don't know what to say.

227
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:14,630
That's normal.

228
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:17,030
You can use simple and clear sentences.

229
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:17,990
Like what?

230
00:10:17,990 --> 00:10:21,750
For example, today I'm working on preparing the presentation,

231
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:24,630
or I've just finished reviewing the documents.

232
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:26,190
That sounds easy to use.

233
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:29,030
Yes, and if you want to talk about future tasks,

234
00:10:29,030 --> 00:10:32,630
you can say, next I will start working on the new project.

235
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:33,670
That's helpful.

236
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:34,810
I'll try that.

237
00:10:34,810 --> 00:10:38,070
By the way, how do you talk about completed tasks?

238
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:40,150
I usually use past tense.

239
00:10:40,150 --> 00:10:45,070
For example, I completed the report, or I finished updating the files.

240
00:10:45,070 --> 00:10:46,070
That makes sense.

241
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:51,030
You can also say, I've already sent the email, or I've completed the task.

242
00:10:51,030 --> 00:10:52,070
I see.

243
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:53,470
That sounds more natural.

244
00:10:53,470 --> 00:10:56,190
Yes, especially in professional settings.

245
00:10:56,190 --> 00:10:59,670
Tina, what do you say when you have too many tasks?

246
00:10:59,670 --> 00:11:04,950
I usually say, I have a lot on my plates, or I'm quite busy at the moment.

247
00:11:04,950 --> 00:11:07,630
I like that expression, on my plate.

248
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:09,670
It's very common in the workplace.

249
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:12,550
What if you can't finish everything on time?

250
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:14,310
Then I communicate early.

251
00:11:14,310 --> 00:11:17,510
I might say, I may not be able to finish this today.

252
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,310
Can we extend the deadline?

253
00:11:19,310 --> 00:11:20,510
That's a good way to handle it.

254
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:22,590
Hey Tina, can you help me with something?

255
00:11:22,590 --> 00:11:23,590
Of course.

256
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:24,590
What do you need?

257
00:11:24,590 --> 00:11:29,430
I'm trying to prioritize my tasks, but I'm not sure which one is more urgent.

258
00:11:29,430 --> 00:11:30,630
Let's take a look.

259
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:31,630
What are your tasks?

260
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:36,950
I need to finish the report, respond to emails, and prepare a presentation.

261
00:11:36,950 --> 00:11:40,790
I'd say the report is the highest priority if it has a deadline.

262
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:42,750
Yes, it's due today.

263
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,690
Then focus on that first.

264
00:11:44,690 --> 00:11:47,030
After that, you can handle the emails.

265
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:48,030
That makes sense.

266
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:50,230
And you can prepare the presentation later.

267
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:51,230
Thanks.

268
00:11:51,230 --> 00:11:52,230
That helps a lot.

269
00:11:52,230 --> 00:11:55,270
Tina, how do you describe your daily tasks in general?

270
00:11:55,270 --> 00:12:01,190
I usually say something like, my main tasks include managing emails, attending meetings,

271
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:02,910
and working on projects.

272
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:04,110
That's a great sentence.

273
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:09,310
You can also say, I'm responsible for organizing files and supporting the team.

274
00:12:09,310 --> 00:12:10,950
That sounds very professional.

275
00:12:10,950 --> 00:12:13,790
Yes, it's useful when introducing your job.

276
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:17,390
Hey, what do you say when you need more time to complete a task?

277
00:12:17,390 --> 00:12:19,590
I try to be polite and clear.

278
00:12:19,590 --> 00:12:23,390
I might say, I need a bit more time to complete this task.

279
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:25,110
That's simple and effective.

280
00:12:25,110 --> 00:12:29,110
Or I'm still working on it and expect to finish it by tomorrow.

281
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:30,630
That's a good way to give an update.

282
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:33,910
Tina, do you ever have to explain tasks and meetings?

283
00:12:33,910 --> 00:12:34,910
All the time.

284
00:12:34,910 --> 00:12:36,190
