I scheduled meetings, followed up on emails,

521
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,600
and reviewed some documents.

522
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:51,160
That's a productive day.

523
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,240
So Tina, when we talk about job tasks,

524
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:57,520
what's the most common question people ask at work?

525
00:23:57,520 --> 00:24:00,800
A very common one is, what are you working on?

526
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:01,960
Let's try that.

527
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,280
Hey Tina, what are you working on right now?

528
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:06,880
I'm currently working on a marketing report.

529
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:09,780
I'm analyzing data and preparing slides.

530
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:11,040
That's a great answer.

531
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:12,600
clear and specific.

532
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:16,880
Yes, it's important to explain your task briefly, but clearly.

533
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:19,840
What if I want to talk about something I completed?

534
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:21,920
Then you can use the past tense.

535
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:25,640
For example, I finished updating the report this morning.

536
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:28,880
Exactly, or I completed the presentation

537
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,440
and sent it to the client.

538
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:31,880
That sounds professional.

539
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:33,720
Yes, it shows progress.

540
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:37,080
Now let's imagine a typical workday conversation.

541
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:38,240
Good morning, Tina.

542
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,000
What tasks do you have today?

543
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Good morning, Leo. Today I need to prepare a report, attend two meetings and respond

544
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:50,280
to emails. That's a busy schedule. Yes, I also need to review some documents before

545
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:56,480
the deadline. Deadlines are always important. Absolutely. Now let's talk about asking about

546
00:24:56,480 --> 00:25:01,960
someone else's tasks. Hey Tina, what's on your plate today? I have quite a few tasks.

547
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:06,960
I'm working on a project update and preparing for a meeting. That's a natural expression.

548
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:11,360
Yes, on your plate means your tasks or responsibilities.

549
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:14,640
Now let's talk about describing tasks in detail.

550
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:18,320
Tina, can you describe your main responsibilities at work?

551
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:24,240
Sure. My main responsibilities include creating content, managing social media,

552
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:26,720
and analyzing campaign performance.

553
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:27,760
That's clear.

554
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:32,720
You can also say, my job involves or I'm responsible for.

555
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:37,600
Let me try. I'm responsible for scheduling meetings and organizing files.

556
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:38,480
Perfect.

557
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:42,640
Now let's talk about ongoing tasks. What are you doing at the moment?

558
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:47,680
I'm working on a client proposal. I'm gathering information and drafting the document.

559
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:48,400
Nice.

560
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:52,640
You can also say I'm in the middle of for tasks in progress.

561
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:55,520
Like I'm in the middle of preparing a report.

562
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:56,640
Exactly.

563
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:59,040
Now let's talk about multitasking.

564
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:02,160
Tina, are you working on multiple tasks today?

565
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:05,800
Yes, I'm handling several tasks at the same time.

566
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:09,040
I'm replying to emails while preparing a presentation.

567
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,560
That sounds stressful.

568
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:13,040
It can be, but it's common at work.

569
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:15,960
Now let's talk about prioritizing tasks.

570
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:18,680
How do you decide which task to do first?

571
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:22,380
I usually prioritize urgent tasks and deadlines.

572
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:23,800
So you might say,

573
00:26:23,800 --> 00:26:27,160
I need to finish this report first because it's urgent.

574
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:28,360
Exactly.

575
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:31,320
Now let's talk about asking for help with tasks.

576
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:33,800
Hey Tina, could you help me with this task?

577
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,280
Sure, what do you need?

578
00:26:35,280 --> 00:26:37,600
I'm not sure how to organize this data.

579
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:39,520
No problem, I can show you.

580
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:41,040
Thanks, I appreciate it.

581
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,000
Any time.

582
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,800
Now what if you're busy?

583
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:46,720
I could say I'm a bit busy right now.

584
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:48,000
Can I help you later?

585
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,040
That's polite.

586
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,200
Yes, always be respectful.

587
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,760
Now let's talk about updating your boss.

588
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:56,560
Tina, can you give me an update on your tasks?

589
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:58,840
Sure, I've completed the report

590
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:01,280
and I'm currently working on the presentation.

591
00:27:01,280 --> 00:27:02,720
That's a good update.

592
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:04,920
You can also mention what's next.

593
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:08,040
Like next I'll start working on the client proposal.

594
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:09,200
Exactly.

595
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,440
Now let's talk about delays.

596
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:14,180
What if you can't finish a task on time?

597
00:27:14,180 --> 00:27:15,960
You should inform your boss.

598
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:19,120
For example, I'm having some delays with this task.

599
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:20,920
I may need more time.

600
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:21,920
Perfect.

601
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:24,240
Now let's talk about completing tasks.

602
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:26,520
Tina, did you finish your task?

603
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:28,960
Yes, I completed it this morning.

604
00:27:28,960 --> 00:27:31,160
Or I've just finished the report.

605
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,160
Exactly.

606
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:34,920
Now let's talk about delegating tasks.

607
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:37,520
Tina, can you assign tasks to others?

608
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:39,160
Yes, sometimes.

609
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,160
What do you say?

610
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,880
Could you handle this task?

611
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:43,880
Or can you take care of this?

612
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:45,280
That's clear and polite.

613
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:46,280
Yes.

614
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:48,280
Now let's talk about teamwork.

615
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:50,280
Are you working on any team tasks?

616
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:53,720
Yes, I'm collaborating with my team on a project.

617
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:55,560
What do you say in that situation?

618
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:58,360
We're working together to complete the project.

619
00:27:58,360 --> 00:28:01,080
Or we're sharing tasks to finish faster.

620
00:28:01,080 --> 00:28:02,280
Exactly.

621
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:05,680
Now let's create a longer real-life conversation.

622
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:08,000
Hey Tina, what are you working on today?

623
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,760
I'm working on a project report

624
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:12,120
and preparing for a meeting this afternoon.

625
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:13,640
Have you started the report?

626
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:15,880
Yes, I've completed the first section

627
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:17,520
and I'm working on the second part.

628
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:18,800
Do you need any help?

629
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:20,080
Actually, yes.

630
00:28:20,080 --> 00:28:21,800
Could you review my draft?

631
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:23,200
Sure, I'll take a look.

632
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,840
Thanks, I appreciate it.

633
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:26,000
When is the deadline?

634
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,920
It's tomorrow, so I need to finish it today.

635
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:29,880
That's tight.

636
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:32,360
Yes, I'm trying to stay focused.

637
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:33,760
What about your meeting?

638
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:36,400
I need to prepare slides and gather data.

639
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:38,080
Sounds like a busy day.

640
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:39,960
It is, but I'm managing.

641
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:41,520
Let me know if you need anything.

642
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:42,800
I will, thanks.

643
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:43,620
Later.

644
00:28:43,620 --> 00:28:45,720
Hey, Tina, how's your report going?

645
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,680
It's going well.

646
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:48,160
I've almost finished it.

647
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:48,840
Great.

648
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:51,280
I just need to review it before sending.

649
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:52,440
Good idea.

650
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,520
What about you?

651
00:28:53,520 --> 00:28:55,520
I've completed my tasks for the day.

652
00:28:55,520 --> 00:28:56,440
That's nice.

653
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:57,480
End of day.

654
00:28:57,480 --> 00:28:58,760
I'm done with my tasks.

655
00:28:58,760 --> 00:28:59,680
I'm heading out.

656
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:02,320
Same here. It was a productive day.

657
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:04,400
Yes. We accomplished a lot.

658
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,360
Definitely.

659
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:09,200
So, Tina, what's the key to talking about job tasks?

660
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:12,080
Be clear, specific, and organized.

661
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:14,000
And use simple sentences.

662
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:17,280
Yes. Clarity is more important than complexity.

663
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:18,240
All right, everyone.

664
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:22,560
We hope this conversation helps you describe your job tasks confidently.

665
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:25,280
Keep practicing these phrases in your daily work.

666
00:29:25,280 --> 00:29:26,320
Thanks for listening.

667
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:27,440
See you next time.

668
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:28,080
Goodbye.

669
00:29:28,080 --> 00:29:28,800
Bye.

670
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:33,360
Welcome back to Business English Podcast. Hello and thanks for listening today.

671
00:29:33,360 --> 00:29:37,600
I'm Daniel. Welcome everyone. Let's begin today's English conversation.

672
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:42,560
And I'm Sophia. We're here to help you learn natural conversational English.

673
00:29:42,560 --> 00:29:48,640
Our goal is to make English learning practical, clear, and easy to use in your daily work life.

674
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:53,840
Today we have a very important and practical topic. We're going to talk about how to talk

675
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:55,960
about job tasks in English.

676
00:29:55,960 --> 00:30:01,040
Yes, this is extremely useful because every day at work you need to explain what you are

677
00:30:01,040 --> 00:30:04,840
doing, what you have done, and what you will do next.

678
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:05,840
Exactly.

679
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:10,300
Whether you are talking to your boss, your coworkers, or even in meetings, you always

680
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:12,840
need to describe your tasks clearly.

681
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:17,840
And sometimes this can be difficult, especially if English is not your first language.

682
00:30:17,840 --> 00:30:21,360
You might know the task, but you don't know how to explain it.

683
00:30:21,360 --> 00:30:26,220
That's why today, we're going to give you a full conversation with many real life examples

684
00:30:26,220 --> 00:30:28,360
so you can sound natural and confident.

685
00:30:28,360 --> 00:30:32,260
Alright, Daniel, let's start with a simple situation.

686
00:30:32,260 --> 00:30:36,800
Imagine you just arrived at work and your co-worker asks you what you're doing today.

687
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:37,800
Good starting point.

688
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:38,960
Hey, Sophia.

689
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:39,960
Good morning.

690
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:41,040
What are you working on today?

691
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:42,240
Good morning, Daniel.

692
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:45,480
Today I'm focusing on preparing the monthly report.

693
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:50,560
I also need to reply to some client emails and attend a meeting in the afternoon.

694
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:53,840
a perfect answer. You clearly explained your tasks.

695
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:57,840
Yes, and notice how I used simple verbs like preparing,

696
00:30:57,840 --> 00:31:03,040
replying, and attending. These are very common when talking about job tasks.

697
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:06,320
Let's break it down more. When you talk about your tasks,

698
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:09,920
you can say, I'm working on or I need to.

699
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:13,440
Exactly. For example, I'm working on a presentation

700
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,840
or I need to finish a report.

701
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:19,680
Let's continue the conversation. That sounds like a busy day.

702
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:20,800
When is your meeting?

703
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:22,640
It's scheduled for 3pm.

704
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:25,280
I need to prepare some notes before that.

705
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:29,680
Great. You used scheduled, which is very common in work situations.

706
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:32,080
Now let's move to another situation.

707
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:35,520
Imagine your boss asks you for an update on your work.

708
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:37,360
That happens all the time.

709
00:31:37,360 --> 00:31:38,400
Let's try it.

710
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:41,280
Daniel, can you give me an update on the project?

711
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:44,320
Sure. I've completed the first phase of the project,

712
00:31:44,320 --> 00:31:46,640
and I'm currently working on the second phase.

713
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:49,040
I expect to finish everything by Friday.

714
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:54,480
That's an excellent update. It includes what you finished, what you're doing now, and your deadline.

715
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:56,720
Yes, that's a good structure to follow.

716
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:58,800
Now, let's make it more detailed.

717
00:31:58,800 --> 00:31:59,440
Okay.

718
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:02,480
Daniel, can you update me on your tasks today?

719
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:07,680
Of course. This morning, I finalized the budget report and sent it to the finance team.

720
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:13,040
Right now, I'm reviewing the client feedback, and later, I'll be working on revising the proposal.

721
00:32:13,040 --> 00:32:18,080
That sounds very professional. You used past, present, and future naturally.

722
00:32:18,080 --> 00:32:21,160
Yes, that's very important when talking about tasks.

723
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:24,720
Now let's talk about asking someone about their tasks.

724
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:25,640
Good idea.

725
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:28,240
Hey Daniel, what are you currently working on?

726
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:30,760
I'm working on updating the company website.

727
00:32:30,760 --> 00:32:34,080
I need to fix some design issues and upload new content.

728
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:35,880
That's clear and specific.

729
00:32:35,880 --> 00:32:37,200
What about you?

730
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:39,240
I'm handling customer support today.

731
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:42,280
I'm responding to inquiries and resolving some complaints.

732
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:43,720
That's a great example.

733
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:46,560
Now let's move to a more realistic office situation

734
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:48,640
where tasks change during the day.

735
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:50,240
That happens a lot.

736
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,840
Daniel, do you have a minute?

737
00:32:51,840 --> 00:32:53,360
I need your help with something.

738
00:32:53,360 --> 00:32:54,560
Sure, what's up?

739
00:32:54,560 --> 00:32:56,080
I was working on the report,

740
00:32:56,080 --> 00:32:58,560
but I just got a new task from my manager.

741
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:01,120
I need to prepare a presentation by tomorrow.

742
00:33:01,120 --> 00:33:02,800
Oh wow, that's sudden.

743
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:05,920
Yes, so I might need to postpone the report.

744
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:09,040
That's a great phrase, postpone the report.

745
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:11,920
Yes, it means delay or do it later.

746
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:12,960
Let's continue.

747
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:15,360
Do you want me to help you with the presentation?

748
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:16,480
That would be great.

749
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:18,080
Could you help me gather some data?

750
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:19,080
Of course!

751
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,080
I'll take care of that.

752
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:21,580
Perfect teamwork.

753
00:33:21,580 --> 00:33:24,580
Now let's talk about describing routine tasks.

754
00:33:24,580 --> 00:33:27,280
Yes, daily tasks are very common.

755
00:33:27,280 --> 00:33:30,180
Sophia, what do you usually do in your job?

756
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:34,880
I usually start my day by checking emails and organizing my tasks.

757
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:39,280
Then I work on reports, attend meetings, and communicate with clients.

758
00:33:39,280 --> 00:33:41,280
That's a great general description.

759
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:44,980
You can also say, my main responsibilities include.

760
00:33:44,980 --> 00:33:51,980
For example, my main responsibilities include managing schedules, preparing documents, and coordinating with the team.

761
00:33:51,980 --> 00:33:54,980
Exactly. Now let's talk about deadlines.

762
00:33:54,980 --> 00:33:56,980
Deadlines are very important.

763
00:33:56,980 --> 00:33:58,980
Daniel, have you finished the report yet?

764
00:33:58,980 --> 00:34:02,980
Not yet. I'm still working on it, but I'll finish it before the deadline.

765
00:34:02,980 --> 00:34:05,980
Good. What if you can't meet the deadline?

766
00:34:05,980 --> 00:34:07,980
Then you should communicate.

767
00:34:07,980 --> 00:34:08,980
Let's try.

768
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:13,980
Sophia, I wanted to update you. I'm having some difficulties with the task, so I might need an extra day to complete the report.

769
00:34:13,980 --> 00:34:15,580
extra day to complete it.

770
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:18,460
Thanks for letting me know. Please keep me updated.

771
00:34:18,460 --> 00:34:20,460
That's professional communication.

772
00:34:20,460 --> 00:34:22,940
No, let's talk about multitasking.

773
00:34:22,940 --> 00:34:25,260
That's something many people do at work.

774
00:34:25,260 --> 00:34:28,060
Daniel, how do you manage multiple tasks?

775
00:34:28,060 --> 00:34:33,340
I usually prioritize my tasks. I focus on urgent tasks first and then handle the

776
00:34:33,340 --> 00:34:34,620
less important ones.

777
00:34:34,620 --> 00:34:35,980
That's a great answer.

778
00:34:35,980 --> 00:34:36,940
What about you?

779
00:34:36,940 --> 00:34:41,500
I make a to-do list every morning and track my progress throughout the day.

780
00:34:41,500 --> 00:34:43,100
That's very organized.

781
00:34:43,100 --> 00:34:46,260
Now, let's move to explaining completed tasks.

782
00:34:46,260 --> 00:34:48,940
Yes, this is important when reporting your work.

783
00:34:48,940 --> 00:34:51,180
Daniel, what did you complete today?

784
00:34:51,180 --> 00:34:57,060
Today, I finished updating the database, sent out emails to clients, and prepared the meeting agenda.

785
00:34:57,060 --> 00:34:57,940
Perfect.

786
00:34:57,940 --> 00:35:00,300
You can also say, I've completed.

787
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:03,900
For example, I've completed the task you assigned to me.

788
00:35:03,900 --> 00:35:06,380
Now let's talk about problems with tasks.

789
00:35:06,380 --> 00:35:08,620
Yes, this is very realistic.

790
00:35:08,620 --> 00:35:12,220
Sophia, I ran into an issue while working on the project.

791
00:35:12,220 --> 00:35:13,420
What kind of issue?

792
00:35:13,420 --> 00:35:17,180
I couldn't access the data I needed, so it delayed my progress.

793
00:35:17,180 --> 00:35:19,740
I see. Let's try to solve it together.

794
00:35:19,740 --> 00:35:21,420
That's a great response.

795
00:35:21,420 --> 00:35:24,060
Now let's talk about delegating tasks.

796
00:35:24,060 --> 00:35:26,620
That's when you give tasks to someone else.

797
00:35:26,620 --> 00:35:29,580
Daniel, could you handle the client emails today?

798
00:35:29,580 --> 00:35:31,180
Sure. I'll take care of it.

799
00:35:31,180 --> 00:35:33,340
And I'll focus on the presentation.

800
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:34,700
That's teamwork again.

801
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:39,180
Now let's create a longer, natural conversation combining everything.

802
00:35:39,180 --> 00:35:40,140
Great idea.

803
00:35:40,140 --> 00:35:42,780
Good morning, Daniel. What are you working on today?

804
00:35:42,780 --> 00:35:47,260
Good morning, Sophia. Today I'm focusing on finishing the quarterly report.

805
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:51,420
I also need to attend a meeting and respond to some emails. How about you?

806
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:56,300
I'm working on updating the project plan and preparing a presentation for tomorrow.

807
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:59,820
Sounds like a busy day. Have you started the presentation yet?

808
00:35:59,820 --> 00:36:05,340
Yes, I started it yesterday, but I still need to add some data and finalize the slides.

809
00:36:05,340 --> 00:36:06,780
Let me know if you need help.

810
00:36:06,780 --> 00:36:08,460
Thanks, I appreciate that.

811
00:36:08,460 --> 00:36:11,260
Actually, could you help me review the slides later?

812
00:36:11,260 --> 00:36:12,940
Of course. I'd be happy to.

813
00:36:12,940 --> 00:36:15,980
Great. By the way, have you completed the report?

814
00:36:15,980 --> 00:36:20,380
Almost. I finished most of it this morning. I just need to double-check the numbers.

815
00:36:20,380 --> 00:36:22,380
That's good. When is the deadline?

816
00:36:22,380 --> 00:36:24,060
It's due by the end of the day.

817
00:36:24,060 --> 00:36:25,420
You still have time?

818
00:36:25,420 --> 00:36:28,780
Yes, but I want to finish it early so I can focus on the meeting.

819
00:36:28,780 --> 00:36:31,340
That's a good plan. What is the meeting about?

820
00:36:31,340 --> 00:36:33,020
It's about project updates.

821
00:36:33,020 --> 00:36:36,540
I need to explain what I've done so far and what I'll do next.

822
00:36:36,540 --> 00:36:38,940
That's exactly what we're practicing today.

823
00:36:38,940 --> 00:36:40,700
Yes, it's very useful.

824
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:42,860
After the meeting, what will you work on?

825
00:36:42,860 --> 00:36:46,540
I'll probably start working on the new project assigned by my manager.

826
00:36:46,540 --> 00:36:48,460
Sounds good. What about you?

827
00:36:48,460 --> 00:36:52,860
After I finish the presentation, I'll focus on responding to client requests.

828
00:36:52,860 --> 00:36:54,060
That's important.

829
00:36:54,060 --> 00:36:57,740
Yes, and I also need to follow up on a few tasks from yesterday.

830
00:36:57,740 --> 00:36:59,020
Very productive.

831
00:36:59,020 --> 00:37:03,820
Thanks. This conversation shows how we naturally talk about tasks at work.

832
00:37:03,820 --> 00:37:07,820
Exactly. You just need to practice using simple structures like,

833
00:37:07,820 --> 00:37:11,260
I'm working on, I've completed, and I need to.

834
00:37:11,260 --> 00:37:15,100
And remember to be clear and organized when explaining your tasks.

835
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:18,460
Yes. Clarity is key in workplace communication.

836
00:37:18,460 --> 00:37:21,900
All right. Before we finish, we have a question for our listeners.

837
00:37:21,900 --> 00:37:25,020
What tasks do you do every day at your job?

838
00:37:25,020 --> 00:37:27,740
Try to answer using the phrases you learned today.

839
00:37:27,740 --> 00:37:29,420
Practice makes perfect.

840
00:37:29,420 --> 00:37:31,020
Thank you so much for listening.

841
00:37:31,020 --> 00:37:32,620
See you in the next episode.

842
00:37:32,620 --> 00:37:33,620
Goodbye, everyone.

843
00:37:33,620 --> 00:37:34,900
Bye.

844
00:37:34,900 --> 00:37:37,900
Welcome back to Business English Podcast.

845
00:37:37,900 --> 00:37:40,260
Hello, everyone, and thanks for listening today.

846
00:37:40,260 --> 00:37:41,260
I'm Leo.

847
00:37:41,260 --> 00:37:42,260
And I'm Tina.

848
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:47,660
We're here to help you learn natural, practical English that you can use at work every day.

849
00:37:47,660 --> 00:37:52,020
Our goal is to make English learning simple, useful, and realistic.

850
00:37:52,020 --> 00:37:58,340
Today, we have a very important topic, how to talk about job tasks in English.

851
00:37:58,340 --> 00:38:02,460
Yes, this is something you need to do every single day at work.

852
00:38:02,460 --> 00:38:06,980
You need to explain what you're doing, what you've done, and what you're going to do next.

853
00:38:06,980 --> 00:38:07,980
Exactly.

854
00:38:07,980 --> 00:38:12,660
Whether you're speaking to your manager, your co-workers, or even a client, you need to

855
00:38:12,660 --> 00:38:15,100
describe your tasks clearly.

856
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:19,220
So today, we're going to walk through real conversations where we talk about daily

857
00:38:19,220 --> 00:38:21,620
job tasks in natural English.

858
00:38:21,620 --> 00:38:26,940
We'll also share examples, common phrases, and even some mistakes people make.

859
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:28,620
Alright, are you ready?

860
00:38:28,620 --> 00:38:29,900
Let's get started.

861
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:31,900
So Leo, how are you today?

862
00:38:31,900 --> 00:38:34,660
I'm doing okay, but I'm a bit tired.

863
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:37,020
I had a really busy day yesterday.

864
00:38:37,020 --> 00:38:38,020
Oh really?

865
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:39,380
What were you working on?

866
00:38:39,380 --> 00:38:44,540
I had to finish a report, respond to a lot of emails, and prepare for a meeting.

867
00:38:44,540 --> 00:38:47,020
It felt like everything came at once.

868
00:38:47,020 --> 00:38:48,020
That sounds stressful.

869
00:38:48,020 --> 00:38:49,620
Yeah, it was.

870
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:52,900
But I managed to complete most of my tasks by the end of the day.

871
00:38:52,900 --> 00:38:53,900
That's good.

872
00:38:53,900 --> 00:38:56,980
So, when someone asks you, what are you working on?

873
00:38:56,980 --> 00:38:58,660
How do you usually answer?

874
00:38:58,660 --> 00:39:04,260
I usually say something like, I'm working on a report, or I'm preparing a presentation.

875
00:39:04,260 --> 00:39:08,740
Exactly! That's a very common question at work. Let's practice that.

876
00:39:08,740 --> 00:39:11,380
Hey Leo, what are you working on right now?

877
00:39:11,380 --> 00:39:16,580
I'm working on the monthly sales report. I'm analyzing the data and writing a summary.

878
00:39:16,580 --> 00:39:19,620
That's a great answer. It's clear and specific.

879
00:39:19,620 --> 00:39:24,340
Yes, it's important to explain your task, not just say I'm working.

880
00:39:24,340 --> 00:39:27,380
Right. Let's make it a bit more detailed.

881
00:39:27,380 --> 00:39:29,660
What are you working on this morning?

882
00:39:29,660 --> 00:39:32,020
This morning, I'm reviewing some documents

883
00:39:32,020 --> 00:39:33,820
and updating a spreadsheet.

884
00:39:33,820 --> 00:39:36,300
After that, I'll send an email to the team.

885
00:39:36,300 --> 00:39:37,140
Perfect.

886
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:40,020
You used present continuous and future plans.

887
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:41,500
Very natural.

888
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:42,620
What about you, Tina?

889
00:39:42,620 --> 00:39:44,260
What are you working on today?

890
00:39:44,260 --> 00:39:47,220
Today, I'm focusing on client communication.

891
00:39:47,220 --> 00:39:49,980
I'm replying to emails, scheduling meetings,

892
00:39:49,980 --> 00:39:52,180
and following up on requests.

893
00:39:52,180 --> 00:39:53,580
That sounds busy.

894
00:39:53,580 --> 00:39:56,180
It is, but I like being organized.

895
00:39:56,180 --> 00:40:00,780
Let's talk about something important, explaining completed tasks.

896
00:40:00,780 --> 00:40:05,340
Yes, because at work you often need to report what you've already done.

897
00:40:05,340 --> 00:40:07,820
Exactly. For example, you might say,

898
00:40:07,820 --> 00:40:11,140
I finished the report or I sent the email.

899
00:40:11,140 --> 00:40:13,100
Let's practice a conversation.

900
00:40:13,100 --> 00:40:15,780
Hey Tina, did you complete the presentation?

901
00:40:15,780 --> 00:40:20,140
Yes, I finished it this morning. I also shared it with the team for feedback.

902
00:40:20,140 --> 00:40:22,780
Great. Did you include the latest data?

903
00:40:22,780 --> 00:40:26,580
Yes, I updated all the numbers and added a few charts.

904
00:40:26,580 --> 00:40:28,980
Excellent! That's a clear update.

905
00:40:28,980 --> 00:40:32,280
Now, let's talk about ongoing tasks.

906
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:35,780
Right. Sometimes tasks are not finished yet.

907
00:40:35,780 --> 00:40:37,380
In that case, you can say,

908
00:40:37,380 --> 00:40:40,780
I'm still working on it, or it's in progress.

909
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:41,880
Let's try that.

910
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:44,080
Hey, Leo, is the report ready?

911
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:46,080
Not yet. I'm still working on it.

912
00:40:46,080 --> 00:40:49,280
I've completed the first draft, but I need to review it.

913
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,580
That's a great answer.

914
00:40:50,580 --> 00:40:52,800
You explain the progress clearly.

915
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:55,340
Yes, and it shows responsibility.

916
00:40:55,340 --> 00:40:58,540
Now let's talk about prioritizing tasks.

917
00:40:58,540 --> 00:41:01,620
That's very important when you have a lot of work.

918
00:41:01,620 --> 00:41:02,580
Exactly.

919
00:41:02,580 --> 00:41:05,140
You might say, I'm focusing on this first,

920
00:41:05,140 --> 00:41:07,660
or this is my top priority.

921
00:41:07,660 --> 00:41:09,100
Let's practice.

922
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:11,220
You have three tasks today.

923
00:41:11,220 --> 00:41:13,020
What are you doing first?

924
00:41:13,020 --> 00:41:15,420
I'm focusing on the urgent report first,

925
00:41:15,420 --> 00:41:17,180
because the deadline is today.

926
00:41:17,180 --> 00:41:18,940
Then I'll work on emails.

927
00:41:18,940 --> 00:41:22,180
Perfect. You explained your priorities clearly.

928
00:41:22,180 --> 00:41:25,060
Now let's talk about asking about tasks.

929
00:41:25,060 --> 00:41:28,940
Yes, sometimes you need to ask your coworker what they're doing.

930
00:41:28,940 --> 00:41:33,460
For example, what are you working on? Or have you completed this task?

931
00:41:33,460 --> 00:41:34,860
Let's practice.

932
00:41:34,860 --> 00:41:38,100
Hey Tina, have you started working on the new project?

933
00:41:38,100 --> 00:41:42,940
Yes, I've started. I'm currently gathering information and planning the structure.

934
00:41:42,940 --> 00:41:44,380
That's a great update.

935
00:41:44,380 --> 00:41:45,300
Thanks.

936
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:48,500
Now let's talk about delegating tasks.

937
00:41:48,500 --> 00:41:52,920
Yes, this is important if you're working in a team or managing others.

938
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:57,640
You might say, can you handle this task or could you take care of this?

939
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:58,640
Let's practice.

940
00:41:58,640 --> 00:42:01,960
Hey, Tina, could you take care of the client emails today?

941
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:03,240
Sure, no problem.

942
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:05,000
I'll handle them this afternoon.

943
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:06,960
Thanks, I appreciate it.

944
00:42:06,960 --> 00:42:07,960
Any time.

945
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:10,520
Now, let's talk about deadlines.

946
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:13,880
Yes, deadlines are a big part of work.

947
00:42:13,880 --> 00:42:19,120
You might say, the deadline is tomorrow, or, I need to finish this by Friday.

948
00:42:19,120 --> 00:42:20,120
Let's practice.

949
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:22,720
When do you need to complete this task?

950
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:24,840
I need to finish it by the end of the day.

951
00:42:24,840 --> 00:42:25,840
It's quite urgent.

952
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:26,840
Okay.

953
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:28,160
Let me know if you need help.

954
00:42:28,160 --> 00:42:29,160
Thanks.

955
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:30,160
I will.

956
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:32,840
Now, let's talk about problems with tasks.

957
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:33,840
Yes.

958
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:36,260
Sometimes things don't go as planned.

959
00:42:36,260 --> 00:42:39,720
In that case, you need to explain the issue clearly.

960
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:43,240
For example, I'm having some trouble with the data analysis.

961
00:42:43,240 --> 00:42:45,360
I've encountered a problem.

962
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:46,360
Let's practice.

963
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:50,520
Hey, Leo, I'm having some trouble with the data analysis.

964
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:52,200
What seems to be the problem?

965
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:55,200
The numbers don't match, and I'm not sure why.

966
00:42:55,200 --> 00:42:56,640
Let's take a look together.

967
00:42:56,640 --> 00:42:57,640
Thanks.

968
00:42:57,640 --> 00:42:59,120
I really appreciate your help.

969
00:42:59,120 --> 00:43:00,120
No problem.

970
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:03,280
Now let's talk about giving updates to your manager.

971
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:07,260
Yes, this is very important in professional communication.

972
00:43:07,260 --> 00:43:12,320
You might say, I wanted to give you an update, or here's the progress so far.

973
00:43:12,320 --> 00:43:13,320
Let's practice.

974
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:16,480
Hi, I wanted to give you an update on the project.

975
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:18,120
Sure, go ahead.

976
00:43:18,120 --> 00:43:21,840
I've completed the research phase and started working on the draft.

977
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:24,440
I expect to finish it by Thursday.

978
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:26,600
That's a clear and professional update.

979
00:43:26,600 --> 00:43:27,600
Thank you.

980
00:43:27,600 --> 00:43:30,240
Now, let's talk about multitasking.

981
00:43:30,240 --> 00:43:34,360
Yes, sometimes you have to do many tasks at once.

982
00:43:34,360 --> 00:43:40,200
You might say, I'm handling multiple tasks, or I'm juggling several projects.

983
00:43:40,200 --> 00:43:41,200
Let's practice.

984
00:43:41,200 --> 00:43:42,880
How's your workload today?

985
00:43:42,880 --> 00:43:46,960
I'm quite busy. I'm juggling several tasks at the moment.

986
00:43:46,960 --> 00:43:48,320
Sounds like a lot.

987
00:43:48,320 --> 00:43:50,320
It is, but I'm managing.

988
00:43:50,320 --> 00:43:52,880
Now let's talk about finishing work.

989
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:56,800
Yes, it's important to clearly say when a task is done.

990
00:43:56,800 --> 00:44:00,720
You can say I've completed the task or it's all done.

991
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:03,920
Let's practice. Did you finish the report?

992
00:44:03,920 --> 00:44:07,120
Yes, I've completed it and sent it to you for review.

993
00:44:07,120 --> 00:44:08,880
Great. I'll take a look.

994
00:44:08,880 --> 00:44:09,840
Thanks.

995
00:44:09,840 --> 00:44:13,340
Now, let's talk about planning future tasks.

996
00:44:13,340 --> 00:44:15,840
Yes, this helps you stay organized.

997
00:44:15,840 --> 00:44:21,080
You might say, next I'll work on, or I'm planning to.

998
00:44:21,080 --> 00:44:22,280
Let's practice.

999
00:44:22,280 --> 00:44:24,200
What are your plans for tomorrow?

1000
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:27,160
Tomorrow, I'm planning to finalize the presentation

1001
00:44:27,160 --> 00:44:28,840
and prepare for the meeting.

1002
00:44:28,840 --> 00:44:30,680
That sounds like a good plan.

1003
00:44:30,680 --> 00:44:31,600
Thanks.

1004
00:44:31,600 --> 00:44:34,120
Now, let's talk about teamwork.

1005
00:44:34,120 --> 00:44:37,440
Yes, many tasks involve working with others.

1006
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:42,320
You might say, let's work on this together, or we can divide the tasks.

1007
00:44:42,320 --> 00:44:45,600
Let's practice. This project looks big.

1008
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:48,480
Yes, maybe we should divide the tasks.

1009
00:44:48,480 --> 00:44:51,040
Good idea. I'll handle the research.

1010
00:44:51,040 --> 00:44:53,280
And I'll work on the presentation.

1011
00:44:53,280 --> 00:44:54,320
Perfect.

1012
00:44:54,320 --> 00:44:57,440
Now, let's talk about reviewing tasks.

1013
00:44:57,440 --> 00:45:00,480
Yes, checking your work is very important.

1014
00:45:00,480 --> 00:45:05,760
You might say, I need to review this, or I'm double checking the details.

1015
00:45:05,760 --> 00:45:08,480
Let's practice. Is the report ready?

1016
00:45:08,480 --> 00:45:11,440
Almost. I'm just reviewing it one more time.

1017
00:45:11,440 --> 00:45:12,960
That's good practice.

1018
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:15,920
Yes. I want to make sure everything is correct.

1019
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:19,200
Before we finish, let's reflect on what we've learned.

1020
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:24,320
Today, we practiced how to talk about job tasks in many different situations.

1021
00:45:24,320 --> 00:45:29,200
We talked about starting tasks, describing progress, finishing tasks,

1022
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:31,920
handling problems, and planning ahead.

1023
00:45:31,920 --> 00:45:40,560
And we used many useful phrases, like I'm working on, I've completed, I'm still working on it, and I'll finish it by.

1024
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:44,640
Exactly. The more you practice, the more natural they will feel.

1025
00:45:44,640 --> 00:45:48,880
Remember, communication at work is about being clear and professional.

1026
00:45:48,880 --> 00:45:53,040
Don't worry about making mistakes. Just focus on expressing your ideas.

1027
00:45:53,040 --> 00:45:55,760
All right, that's all for today's episode.

1028
00:45:55,760 --> 00:45:57,520
Thank you so much for listening.

1029
00:45:57,520 --> 00:46:00,800
Keep practicing and improving your English every day.

1030
00:46:00,800 --> 00:46:02,800
We'll see you in the next episode.

1031
00:46:02,800 --> 00:46:03,800
Goodbye, everyone.
